      "description": "This is Bilston Central tram stop seen from Hall Street Bridge. The tram waiting at platform two is destined for Wolverhampton St George's. The bus station is adjacent at road level on the left.\nThe Midland Metro opened on 30th May 1999.It is 12½ mile tram-line between Wolverhampton and Birmingham with a short on-street section in Wolverhampton, the rest following the former Great Western Railway trackbed (closed in 1972). The trams are powered by 750 volt DC electric current supplied though overhead power cables.",
